			<div class="content" id="post-content-4863023">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Fiction (as always)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Basic Article Template, interviews only with tests subjects, normal test logs.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Elevator&nbsp;Pitch</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Elevator&nbsp;Pitch</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> What started out as an idea of an anomalous plushie that would do good things became… well, a Safe-Class anomalous old monkey plushie with a simple backstory that protects (physically and emotionally) the ones hugging it <span style="text-decoration: underline;">if</span> they are emotionally linked to the object.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> SCP-#### would be discovered by a field agent accidentally, when a little boy hugging the object was run over by a truck and suffered no damage at all. He (the field agent) would keep an eye on the boy for some months, who seemed to have no anomalous properties. The field agent would become a friend of the boy and his plushie. Months later, the boy would give the plushie to the field agent and make him promise to take care of “him”. He said that he would go to a place called “Imagination” and promised he would send letters to the plushie and to the agent every few weeks. SCP-#### would be brought home by the field agent. After half a year, the boy would be found dead at the roadside. When the field agent, in tears, hugged the object, he would hear a voice calming him down. The man would later survive a stray bullet with no damage at all while he slept hugging the plushie. After that, the field agent would bring the object to the foundation site. This artifact would be kept in a room <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">safe from external groups of interest</span>, only reliable personnel would come into contact with it and SCP-#### would sometimes ask to the ones hugging him to write letters destined to “Imagination”, saying he moved and was being treated well by the Researchers.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Hook/Attention-Grabber</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hook/Attention-Grabber</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">It would be an object protected by the Foundation against some Groups of Interest, who would want to have SCP-#### so they could become invincible.</span> It is a stuffed toy that protects its owner.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;Notes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Additional&nbsp;Notes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Still needs some proofreading because, as the guide says, “as the author you develop a certain blindness to your own writing.” Also needs lots of criticism and some similar SCPs. GOIs removed from the idea.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

