														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4864364">
									

<p>1) How is a Thaumiel-class hazard? It sounds more like a Safe SCP (easy to secure, generally beneficial SCP). You don't want to over-sell it as a problem.</p>
<p>2) Your Hook should be part of the Central Narrative; your hook is simply that it's a stuffed toy that actually protects its owner, which is a cool idea in and of itself.</p>
<p>3) The stuffed animal obviously has limits; it would be nice to see these limits explored. Also, it apparently has some sapience; it would be interesting to see this guy interact with other kid-friendly SCPs, and the link to &quot;Imagination&quot; may give it something in common with <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1762">SCP-1762</a> &quot;Here Be Dragons&quot;. I know links to other SCPs are frowned on, but in this case they work and enhance the SCP.</p>
<p>Overall, a good concept, but needs some work.</p>

							</div>

								
					
